[CENTER][SIZE=7][B][COLOR=#2f9bff]💧 WaterMc[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=5][B]High-performance Paper-compatible server core for Minecraft 1.21.11[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]Faster restarts · leaner memory · built-in scripting · one-jar migration from Paper, Purpur and Leaf[/SIZE]

[B]Java 21+ · Bukkit / Spigot / Paper plugins · Purpur features · Leaf optimizations[/B][/CENTER]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=6][B]⚡ Why WaterMc[/B][/SIZE]

WaterMc is a fork of [B]Leaf[/B] (and therefore of Paper, Purpur, Gale, Pufferfish and Leaves) for Minecraft [B]1.21.11[/B]. Everything you get from Leaf is still there. WaterMc adds its own work on top: a faster startup path, lower memory use, a built-in script engine, safer data storage, admin tools and a fully automatic migration from other cores.

[LIST]
[*][B]Drop-in replacement.[/B] Put [I]watermc-1.21.11.jar[/I] into your existing server folder and start it. Configs, worlds, bans, ops and whitelists move automatically. Nothing is deleted.
[*][B]Your plugins keep working.[/B] Full Bukkit / Spigot / Paper API. Spigot-mapped plugins are remapped automatically, as on Paper.
[*][B]Honest numbers.[/B] Every benchmark below was measured, with the setup written next to it.
[/LIST]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=6][B]📊 Benchmarks[/B][/SIZE]

[I]Setup: AMD FX-4100 (4 cores), 16 GB RAM, Windows 11, Eclipse Temurin 21.0.12, G1 GC. Both cores run in the same folder layout with the same settings; runs alternate WaterMc / Leaf. Leaf = official Leaf 1.21.11 build.[/I]

[SIZE=5][B]WaterMc vs Leaf[/B][/SIZE]
[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Test[/TH][TH]Leaf[/TH][TH]WaterMc[/TH][TH]Difference[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]Time before the server code starts (launcher, warm restart)[/TD][TD]3.8 – 4.4 s[/TD][TD][B]0.7 – 0.8 s[/B][/TD][TD][COLOR=#2ecc71][B]~3 s saved on every start[/B][/COLOR][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Warm restart to "Done" (flat world, no plugins, 2 GB heap, 3 runs each)[/TD][TD]28.9 s[/TD][TD][B]27.1 s[/B][/TD][TD][COLOR=#2ecc71][B]−6 %[/B][/COLOR] *[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Heap in use after startup (after GC)[/TD][TD]224 MiB[/TD][TD][B]214 MiB[/B][/TD][TD][COLOR=#2ecc71][B]−4 %[/B][/COLOR][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Live heap with 1 600 loaded chunks (same saved world)[/TD][TD]393.2 MiB[/TD][TD][B]385.2 MiB[/B][/TD][TD][COLOR=#2ecc71][B]−2 %[/B][/COLOR][/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]
[SIZE=2]* Measured before the new launcher and lazy mappings were added; both make startup faster on top of this result.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]WaterMc optimizations (before → after, same core)[/B][/SIZE]
[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Scenario[/TH][TH]Before[/TH][TH]After[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]Mob crowd: 600 mobs in one pen, share of the main thread spent on entity pushing[/TD][TD]21 – 25 %[/TD][TD][B]10 – 11 %[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Mixed scene: 1 500 mobs of 9 types with AI, profile hot spots removed[/TD][TD]—[/TD][TD][B]≈ 9 % of the main thread freed[/B][/TD][/TR]
