[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=6][B]🚀 Faster startup[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Own launcher.[/B] The inherited launcher re-read and hashed ~125 MB of libraries on every start. WaterMc's launcher remembers what it already verified and only re-checks files that changed: about 3 seconds saved per restart. If a library is damaged or missing, it is restored from the jar.
[*][B]Lazy mappings.[/B] The 10+ MB name mapping files are no longer parsed on every start. They load only when a plugin actually needs them, in the background, and are released afterwards.
[*][B]Smart plugin remapper[/B], on by default:
[LIST]
[*]API-only plugins are detected and started as they are, without remapping;
[*]plugin jars are hashed once and re-checked only when they change;
[*]the cache moved to [I]plugins/.water-remapped[/I], and an existing [I].paper-remapped[/I] cache is adopted automatically.
[/LIST]
[*][B]Lazy DataFixerUpper[/B] and a headless build: no Swing/AWT console window, no GUI classes loaded.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=6][B]🧠 Lower resource usage[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Entity search without cache misses.[/B] Every chunk section keeps a compact copy of entity hitboxes, so neighbour searches (pushing, mob targeting, AI sensors) no longer jump through thousands of objects. Pushing in dense mob farms became twice as cheap. The comparisons are exactly the same as before, and a live self-check mode confirms it.
[*][B]Neighbour chunk cache.[/B] Pathfinding and collisions near chunk borders no longer miss the chunk cache.
[*][B]Cheaper entity state.[/B] Health is a plain field instead of a synced-data lookup in every alive check.
[*][B]No ghost profiler.[/B] The disabled profiler is no longer registered every tick.
[*][B]Team lookups skipped[/B] for mobs when no mob is in any team.
[*][B]Shared compressed chunk packets[/B] for players watching the same area.
[*][B]Native region compression[/B] (libdeflate) with optional ZSTD.
[*][B]Heap guard:[/B] when memory stays high after GC, cold caches are dropped automatically.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=6][B]🧵 Optional multi-core world ticking[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Each world (overworld, nether, end, minigame or skyblock worlds) ticks on its own CPU thread instead of everything sharing one main thread.
[*]Ideal for servers with several active worlds: lobby + survival, minigame arenas, per-island worlds.
[*]Standard Paper threading for plugins inside a world, so most plugins keep working.
[*]Off by default. Enable it in [I]config/watermc.yml[/I]:
[/LIST]
[CODE]async:
  parallel-world-ticking:
    enabled: true
    threads: 4   # usually the number of busy worlds[/CODE]

[SIZE=6][B]📜 Built-in scripting: WaterScript[/B][/SIZE]
Write simple server logic without a plugin. Put files into [I]scripts/[/I] and run [I]/watermc script reload[/I].
[CODE]command /heal:
    @permission "server.heal"
    player.heal()
    send "&aYou are healed!"

on player_command:
    if line.starts_with("op "):
        cancel
        send "&cUse the console for that."

every 10 minutes:
    broadcast "&bDon't forget to vote!"[/CODE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Events:[/B] join, quit, chat (cancellable), player_command, damage, interact, break, place, death, kill, respawn, world_change, load, unload.
[*]Commands with permissions, aliases and arguments; timers; functions; [I]wait[/I] that never blocks the server.
[*]Persistent [I]$variables[/I], saved safely to disk.
[*]Compiled on load: errors show the file and line immediately.
[*]Sandboxed: an operation limit, and no file, network or reflection access.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=6][B]🔄 Automatic migration from Paper, Spigot, Purpur and Leaf[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Configs move to [I]config/[/I], service data to [I]data/[/I], worlds to [I]worlds/[/I]. If a world folder is locked or the move fails, everything stays where it was.
[*]Leaf and Gale settings are merged into [I]config/watermc.yml[/I]. Configs of other cores are kept untouched in [I]config/legacy/[/I].
[*]ops, whitelist, bans and the user cache are imported into crash-safe storage. The original JSON files are backed up byte for byte before anything changes.
[*]A full report of every move is written to [I]data/upgrade-report-*.txt[/I].
[*][B]Nothing is overwritten or deleted.[/B]
[/LIST]

[SIZE=6][B]🛡️ Safer data[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]ops / whitelist / bans / user cache use an append-only journal with a CRC32C checksum on every record. A crash can never leave a half-written file, and one change means one small write instead of rewriting the whole JSON.
[*]On stop and [I]/save-all flush[/I], player data and journals are written before chunks are flushed.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=6][B]🧰 Admin tools[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][I]/watermc inspect[/I]: top-10 chunks by real tick time, split into entities, block entities and hoppers.
[*][B]Plugin watchdog:[/B] warns when a plugin takes too long in a single tick and names the heaviest class.
[*][I]/watermc drain [host:port][/I]: close logins, transfer players to another server, wait for data writes, then stop.
[*]Built-in [B]Prometheus / JSON metrics[/B] endpoint (off by default).
[*][B]Console in English, Russian or Ukrainian[/B] ([I]misc.console.language[/I]). Log files stay in English, and hosting panels still detect the "Done" line.
[*]Hosting-panel friendly command line: [I]nogui[/I] is accepted, and client-only flags are rejected with a clear message.
[/LIST]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=6][B]📦 Installation[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Install [B]Java 21[/B] or newer.
[*]Stop your server and make a backup (always a good idea).
[*]Replace your server jar with [I]watermc-1.21.11.jar[/I].
[*]Start it: [I]java -Xms4G -Xmx4G -jar watermc-1.21.11.jar --nogui[/I]
[*]Check [I]data/upgrade-report-*.txt[/I] to see what was moved.
[/LIST]
[B]Plugins with a hard-coded path like [I]world/...[/I][/B] (some backup or map plugins) may need their path changed to [I]worlds/world/...[/I]. To keep worlds in the root, start with [I]-Dwatermc.upgrade.move-worlds=false[/I].

[SIZE=6][B]⚙️ Full control[/B][/SIZE]
You stay in control: every WaterMc optimization has its own startup flag, so you can tune the core for your server without editing code.
[SPOILER="Flags"]
[CODE]-Dwatermc.packed-entity-bounds=false      # entity hitbox copies
-Dwatermc.limited-push-query=false        # early-stop push search
-Dwatermc.chunk-cache-neighbourhood=false # 2x2 chunk cache
-Dwatermc.enable-legacy-remapper=false    # plugin remapper (or -Dpaper.disablePluginRemapping=true)
-Dwatermc.remapper.skip-api-only=false    # remap API-only plugins anyway
-Dwatermc.launcher.verify-all=true        # launcher re-hashes every library on each start
-Dwatermc.upgrade.move-worlds=false       # keep worlds in the server root
-Dwatermc.console.language=ru             # console language: en / ru / uk[/CODE]
[/SPOILER]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=6][B]❓ FAQ[/B][/SIZE]
[SPOILER="Will my Paper plugins work?"]Yes. WaterMc implements the same Bukkit / Paper API. Plugins built for Spigot are remapped automatically, as on Paper.[/SPOILER]
[SPOILER="Can I go back to Paper or Leaf?"]Yes. Worlds are standard Anvil worlds: move them back from [I]worlds/[/I]. The original JSON lists are in [I]data/migration-backup/[/I], and your old configs are in [I]config/[/I] and [I]config/legacy/[/I].[/SPOILER]
[SPOILER="Why WaterMc and not Folia?"]Folia changes the server threading model, so most plugins (economy, protection, minigames, menus) need special Folia builds or do not work at all. WaterMc keeps the standard Paper threading, so your whole plugin list works as it is, and you still get every optimization on this page. If you need several CPU cores, turn on [B]multi-core world ticking[/B]: every world gets its own thread, and most plugins keep working.[/SPOILER]
[SPOILER="Which Minecraft version?"]1.21.11, Java Edition. Java 21 or newer is required.[/SPOILER]

